1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,280
Supplier proposals can look
comparable until you read the terms.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,260
DocuMind extracts six commercial fields
from a text-based PDF and records a quote

3
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:12,920
and page number wherever it finds evidence.

4
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:18,580
Here, the vendor, currency, total
amount, delivery and warranty match.

5
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:21,100
Payment terms are flagged for review.

6
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:25,120
The reference says payment
is due 30 days after invoice.

7
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:28,620
The candidate adds acceptance
and invoice approval.

8
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:33,380
The rules leave that relationship to
a person, with both excerpts visible.

9
00:00:33,940 --> 00:00:37,000
Switch to conflicting totals
and open the evidence view.

10
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:42,340
The candidate shows 1200 on
page 1 and 950 on page 2.

11
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:45,280
DocuMind keeps both citations for review.

12
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:48,900
The evaluation used 12 synthetic PDFs.

13
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:52,208
Field F1 was 96.6%.

14
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:56,520
All 72 accepted citations
match the reference evidence.

15
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:02,720
Controlled rules raised comparison accuracy
from 58 to 60 of 66 field decisions

16
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:04,900
and sent more cases to review.

17
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:07,600
Those results describe the synthetic set.

18
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:11,080
New PDFs are processed through
the local command line.

19
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:15,542
Open the public demo to inspect the
examples and download their evidence.
